      'An entire beloved genre in which no one saves the world, no one confesses, nothing is at stake — just the meal, the walk, the afternoon, rendered with total loving attention. The belief that the ordinary is enough is the quietest thing this medium holds, and the closing note of a series that began with the bomb.',
